# GitHub — Mundoria organization only

## Remote

- **Always push to the organization repo:** `git@github.com:MundoriaTech/mundoria.git` (`origin`).
- Do **not** push to `personal` (`MarithaMiracle/cleanscape` or similar) unless the user explicitly asks.
- Before pushing, confirm `origin` points to `MundoriaTech/mundoria`.

## Collaborators & commit identity

- **Never** add Cursor, Cursor Agent, `cursoragent`, cursor bots, or any AI/automation account as a repository collaborator.
- **Never** push commits authored by Cursor Cloud/Background Agent — those appear as `cursoragent` (or similar) on GitHub's contributor graph and cannot be "uninvited"; they come from commit authorship.
- **Always commit and push with your identity:** `Maritha Miracle <marithamiracle@gmail.com>`.
- Use local git commits only; do not use Cursor's "push to GitHub" / cloud agent publish if it uses a bot account.
- If a Cursor-related account appears on the repo, remove it from **Settings → Collaborators** and uninstall the **Cursor GitHub App** under **Settings → Integrations → Applications** (org owner may be required).
- Do not invite GitHub Apps or bots to the repo unless the user explicitly requests it.

## No Cursor commit attribution (mandatory)

- **Never** add `Co-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>` (or any Cursor/cursoragent trailer) to commit messages or PRs.
- After every `git commit`, verify the message has **no** Cursor co-author / "Made with Cursor" trailer. If the environment injected one and the commit is still local (not pushed), amend once to remove it.
- Do not use `--trailer` flags that attribute work to Cursor.
- Author and committer must both be `Maritha Miracle <marithamiracle@gmail.com>` only.

## Pull requests

- Create PRs against `MundoriaTech/mundoria`, not the personal fork.
